ORACLE 2: SciPy / NumPy
-----------------------
- Tools   : SciPy 1.17.0 and NumPy 2.4.1 (both BSD-3-Clause), under Python 3.14.2 on
            macOS/arm64. Not vendored; not needed at test run time.
- Used for: scipy.stats.norm.isf (Phi^-1, Cephes ndtri) for the Bonferroni detector
            multiplier; scipy.stats.norm.sf (Cephes ndtr) for each integrity-risk tail
            term; scipy.optimize.brentq for the protection-level root;
            numpy.linalg.inv (LAPACK getrf/getri) as a third independent inverse of
            every normal matrix.
- The largest RTKLIB-vs-LAPACK disagreement over every hypothesis geometry in the
  committed fixture is measured by the generator and printed into the fixture header.


INPUT GEOMETRY (MODELLED, shared with kshana on purpose)
--------------------------------------------------------
kshana's illustrative Moonlight/LCNS-class constellation
(`lunar_service::LunarConstellation::illustrative_lcns`) reduced to Moon-fixed
coordinates and filtered by the elevation mask, at seven service-volume points:
south-polar (the Artemis target region), mid-latitude, equatorial and a raised
highland site; 6 to 19 satellites in view; sigma_URE 10 / 30 / 60 m; P_HMI 1e-3 to
1e-7. The constellation parameters are illustrative public-source approximations of
the system CLASS -- not the real Moonlight/LCNS ephemeris, and implying no
affiliation, endorsement, heritage, certification or TRL. Re-deriving them inside the
oracle would only re-implement kshana, so they are passed in as given numbers; the
Rust test's `the_fixture_geometry_is_still_the_engines_own_service_volume` proves the
committed geometry is still the geometry the engine produces.


TOLERANCES AND MEASURED AGREEMENT
---------------------------------
Measured over the committed fixture (printed by the tests themselves):
  protection level    worst |delta| 1.061e-8 m (HPL) and 1.044e-8 m (VPL) against a
                      1e-6 m tolerance, on protection levels of 1.7e2 to 6.9e3 m
  dilution of precision worst relative |delta| 1.790e-14 against a 1e-9 tolerance
  detector multiplier worst relative |delta| 2.716e-11 against a 1e-10 tolerance
  RTKLIB vs LAPACK inverse  1.112e-12 relative, over every hypothesis geometry
Three negative controls prove the comparison is not vacuous: a 5 km shift of one
satellite, a 1e-6 relative increase in sigma_URE, and a 0.1 % tightening of P_HMI each
move the protection level by at least 1.7e-4 m -- more than two orders of magnitude
outside the tolerance -- and the tests assert that they do.
